  "title": "Nobel Peace Prize in 2026: Navi Pillay and the ICC",
  "summary": "Navi Pillay, a Nobel Peace Prize winner, was awarded the 2026 prize, following the Trump administration's sanctions on the International Court of Justice (ICJ). The sanctions were criticized as undermining international law and sovereignty. The prize was also linked to a broader conflict resolution effort by the US in India-Pakistan.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Navi Pillay won the 2026 Nobel Peace Prize for her work on human rights and justice.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The US imposed sanctions on ICC President Tomoko Akane and her lawyer Abdoulaye Seye, citing concerns over the tribunal’s application of its jurisdiction.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The Trump administration criticized the Norwegian Nobel Committee for awarding the prize to Navi Pillay.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
